Z||000000||x cuda man||01-05-2000||03:40 AM||||can someone tell me the difference(if any)in the spoilers? the car i just bought has the holes but no spoiler,after market won't work here,it's got to be the real thing.(i guess it was ripped off)any help would be greatly app. thanks.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||01-05-2000||05:38 AM||||The stock spoiler was the same for all Fieros.  The mounting holes were slightly different, though.  A stock spoiler has 4 studs on the bottom of the stands that unscrew.  There are 6 holes.  This way you can move the studs to compensate for the difference in mounting hole location.  Actually, this probably isn't true on spoilers found on cars built before the fastbacks came out as there wasn't any reason for a 2nd set of mounting holes yet.  If you have a notchback any should work.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||01-05-2000||05:40 AM||||All Fiero spoilers are basically identical.  There are a few minor differnces though....the '84 INDY and '85 GT are designed for only notchback Fieros (since there wasn't a fastback yet). <P>The '86-'88 spoilers have different stanchions that allow you to "choose" which Fiero it can go on....either a fastback or notchback.  The fastbacks have a wider spacing on the studs than the notchback. The later stanchions have 3 stud mounting holes....the inner 2 are for notchbacks and the outer 2 are for fastbacks.<P>Aside from the 2 different stanchions (stands) used, the spoilers are identical.<P>If you have to swap the studs around do it very carefully....the stands break very easily and are impossible to find.    ||||reg||1
